Well, to elaborate, "Be careful transporting that, it's made of class"
means to be careful not to break it- the danger is to the the object.
Whereas "Be careful, the stove is hot" means to be careful interacting with
it- the danger is to you.

So, basically the difference is whether the person you're talking to is the
lo ckape or the lo se ckape, approximately.


